  <!-- ============ WHO WE ARE ============ -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="section-inner readable">
      <h2 class="section-title">Who We Are</h2>
      <div class="legal-content">
        <p>{{ settings.title }} is a small, independently run wallpaper library. We're not trying to be the biggest wallpaper site on the internet — there are plenty of those already, packed with thousands of low-effort uploads and duplicate content. Instead, we're trying to be one of the most carefully put-together ones. Every single wallpaper in our library is chosen by hand, checked at full resolution, and sorted into a category before it ever goes live.</p>
        <p>That means our catalog is smaller than the massive stock-photo wallpaper dumps you'll find elsewhere, and we're completely fine with that. We'd rather you spend two minutes browsing a collection where almost everything is worth downloading than twenty minutes scrolling past upscaled, watermarked, or poorly cropped images to find one decent option.</p>
        <p>We started {{ settings.title }} because we were tired of that exact problem — searching for a wallpaper and ending up with a blurry image stretched past its real resolution, or a "4K" wallpaper that clearly wasn't. So we built the site we wished existed: quality over quantity, real resolutions, and wallpapers that are actually described properly instead of dumped with a generic filename.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHAT YOU GET ============ -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align: center;">What You Get</h2>
      <div class="feature-grid" style="margin-top: 28px;">

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-card-number">1</span>
          <h3>True resolution wallpapers</h3>
          <p>No fake 4K. Every wallpaper is checked at its native resolution before publishing — no upscaling, no stretched pixels pretending to be sharp.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-card-number">2</span>
          <h3>Multiple resolutions</h3>
          <p>Most wallpapers come with a few resolution options — 4K, 2K, and Full HD — so you can pick what actually fits your screen.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-card-number">3</span>
          <h3>Desktop and mobile crops</h3>
          <p>Wallpapers are optimized separately for wide desktop displays and tall phone screens, not just one image stretched to fit both.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-card-number">4</span>
          <h3>No signup, no limits</h3>
          <p>Every download is free, with no account required and no artificial daily download cap standing between you and your wallpaper.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-card-number">5</span>
          <h3>Written descriptions</h3>
          <p>Each wallpaper includes a short, real description — where it might look best, what mood it fits, and what to expect from the colors.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <span class="feature-card-number">6</span>
          <h3>Weekly new drops</h3>
          <p>New wallpapers are added on a steady weekly schedule, so the library keeps growing without ever feeling flooded.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HOW WE CURATE ============ -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="section-inner readable">
      <h2 class="section-title">How We Curate</h2>
      <div class="steps-list" style="margin-top: 8px;">

        <div class="step-item">
          <h3>Sourcing</h3>
          <p>We look for images with strong composition, good lighting, and colors that hold up well as a background rather than a standalone photo.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="step-item">
          <h3>Checking at full resolution</h3>
          <p>Every candidate is opened at its native resolution and checked for compression artifacts, banding, noise, and anything that would look bad blown up across a screen.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="step-item">
          <h3>Categorizing and describing</h3>
          <p>Once approved, a wallpaper is sorted into the right category, tagged, and given a short written description before it's published.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ OUR STANDARDS ============ -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="section-inner readable">
      <h2 class="section-title">Our Standards</h2>
      <div class="legal-content">
        <p>We hold every wallpaper in the library to a few basic standards before it's allowed to go live:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Resolution minimums.</strong> Desktop wallpapers are expected to meet at least Full HD (1920×1080), with most reaching 4K (3840×2160) or higher. Mobile wallpapers are checked against common flagship phone resolutions.</li>
          <li><strong>File quality.</strong> We reject images with visible compression artifacts, excessive noise, or obvious upscaling from a smaller source.</li>
          <li><strong>Copyright respect.</strong> We only publish wallpapers we have the rights to share, whether that's original work, properly licensed stock imagery, or content released under a license that permits redistribution. If you believe something on the site infringes your copyright, see our <a href="/dmca/" style="color: var(--accent);">DMCA page</a> for how to reach us.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

